  "dct:title": "Vol.8 Ch.56 — 再会：ラクラン",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 8: Fruit",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol08-ch56",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Lachlan is the astronaut from Ch.15. He spent years in space and lost the ability to feel weather. Rain, wind, cold -- they became abstract data in a suit readout. Tamaki walked with him in rain. Just walked. No technique, no framework. Just the feeling of water on skin. And now he writes: he walked in rain. Finally. On his own. Not in a session, not with a guide -- alone, freely, choosing to be wet and cold and alive. He's volunteering at a children's science center. Teaching kids about Earth -- the planet he had to relearn. The letter is enough. He doesn't need to appear. The handwriting is the presence.",
      "ja": "ラクランは第15話の宇宙飛行士。何年も宇宙にいて天候を感じる能力を失った。雨、風、寒さ。すべてスーツの計器の抽象的なデータになった。環は彼と雨の中を歩いた。ただ歩いた。技法もフレームワークもない。肌に水を感じること。そして今、手紙を書く。雨の中を歩いた。ついに。一人で。セッションではなく、ガイドなしで。一人で、自由に、濡れて寒くて生きていることを選んで。子どもの科学センターでボランティアをしている。子どもたちに地球について教えている。学び直さなければならなかった惑星。手紙で十分。本人が現れる必要はない。手書きが存在。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "The letter as medium. In an age of instant communication, a handwritten letter is a deliberate anachronism -- an act of embodiment. The hand that wrote these words pressed against paper. The ink is physical. Lachlan, who lost touch with the physical world, chooses the most physical form of communication. And the photograph: surrounded by children, pointing at a model of Earth. Not looking at Earth from outside anymore -- standing on it, inside it, teaching others to love it. Heidegger's dwelling: to dwell is not merely to occupy space but to be at home in the world. Lachlan is finally dwelling. Nei's insight -- 'freedom is not isolation' -- is the inverse of Lachlan's astronaut experience. He was free in space. But freedom without ground is just floating.",
      "ja": "媒体としての手紙。即時通信の時代に手書きの手紙は意図的な時代錯誤。身体化の行為。この言葉を書いた手が紙に押し付けられた。インクは物質的。物理世界との接触を失ったラクランが、最も物質的なコミュニケーション形態を選ぶ。そして写真：子どもたちに囲まれ、地球の模型を指差す。もう外から地球を見ていない。その上に、その中に立ち、他者にそれを愛することを教えている。ハイデガーの住まうこと：住まうとは単に空間を占めることではなく、世界の中で家にいること。ラクランはついに住まっている。Neiの洞察「自由は孤立ではない」はラクランの宇宙飛行士体験の逆。宇宙では自由だった。しかし地盤のない自由はただ漂うだけ。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        { "gh:target": "chapter:15", "note": "Lachlan's session. Walking in rain. Relearning Earth." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:55", "note": "Previous reunion: Sora." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:54", "note": "The painter's canvas -- now joined by Lachlan's photo on the office board." },
        { "gh:target": "motif:fruit-ripening", "note": "The tree's fruit is ripe at chapter's end. The reunions are complete. The harvest is near." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. One fruit nearly ripe. Golden. It catches the light differently from the others -- warmer, heavier, ready. The branch bends gently under its weight.",
            "ja": "木。一つの果実がほぼ熟している。金色。他とは違う光の受け方。より温かく、より重く、準備ができている。枝がその重みでわずかにたわむ。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "An envelope on Tamaki's desk. Handwritten address -- careful, slightly unsteady letters. International postmark. The handwriting of someone who relearned how to hold a pen after years of touchscreens and zero gravity.",
            "ja": "環の机の上の封筒。手書きの宛名。丁寧で、わずかに不安定な文字。国際消印。タッチスクリーンと無重力の年月を経て、ペンの持ち方を学び直した人の筆跡。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki reads the letter aloud. Nei listens beside her. The office is quiet. Spring light. The painter's canvas on the wall behind them. Tamaki holds the letter carefully, as if it weighs more than paper.",
            "ja": "環が手紙を声に出して読む。Neiがそばで聴いている。オフィスは静か。春の光。背後の壁に画家のキャンバス。環は手紙を丁寧に持っている。紙以上の重みがあるかのように。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "'Dear Mizuno-san. I walked in rain last week. Finally. It was everything I remembered. Lachlan.'", "ja": "「水野さんへ。先週、雨の中を歩きました。ようやく。覚えていた通りのすべてでした。ラクラン。」" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "A photograph enclosed with the letter. Lachlan at a children's science center. Surrounded by kids -- five, six years old, faces bright with wonder. He is pointing at a model of Earth, blue and white and fragile. He is smiling. Not the careful, distant smile of an astronaut on camera. A real smile. Grounded.",
            "ja": "手紙に同封された写真。子どもの科学センターのラクラン。子どもたちに囲まれている。五歳、六歳、驚きに輝く顔。地球の模型を指差している。青と白、脆い。笑っている。カメラの前の宇宙飛行士の慎重で距離を置いた笑顔ではない。本物の笑顔。地に足がついている。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up, Nei. Quiet. The understanding that freedom and connection are not opposites. That you can orbit the Earth and still need to stand on it.",
            "ja": "クローズアップ、Nei。静か。自由とつながりは対立しないという理解。地球を周回しても、その上に立つ必要があるということ。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "Thank you. You showed me that freedom is not isolation.", "ja": "ありがとう。自由は孤立ではないと、教えてくれた。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki pins the photograph to the office board. Next to the painter's canvas on the wall. Two pieces of evidence that the work matters. That people walked away and kept walking.",
            "ja": "環が写真をオフィスのボードにピンで留める。壁の画家のキャンバスの隣に。仕事が意味を持つという二つの証拠。人々は歩き去り、歩き続けた。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:label": "Seed (closing)",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. The fruit is ripe. Ready. Golden, heavy, warm in the last light. The branch holds. No text.",
            "ja": "木。果実が熟した。準備ができた。金色で重く、最後の光の中で温かい。枝は持ちこたえている。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
